      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I know, and it annoys me a little.\n\nAs the buffer size is a power of two, we could store integer indices, and let the indices run all the way to 32-bit wrapping, while masking all but the lowest bits every time one of the indices were used to index into the array.  That may not be such a bad idea, since it would also eliminate any timing jitter from the conditional wraparound logic.  (Maybe what I describe is actually how cyclic buffers are usually implemented, I just did not know about it.)",
