      "writtenOn": "2024-02-07T03:36:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, this is the \"Bit set/reset\" register, which allows setting or clearing any of the 16 bits of the output register without touching the rest, and without needing a read/modify/write roundtrip.  A one in any of the lower 16 bits will set the corresponding output to one, a one in any of the upper 16 bits will set the corresponding output to zero.",
